2.5","slug":"val-tl-negc-2026-10-25-total-games-2pt5","sportsMarketType":"totals","groupItemTitle":"O/U 2.5 Games","line":2.5,"description":"This market refers to the Valorant Lower Bracket Round 1 match between Team Liquid Brazil and Nova Esports GC in the VCT Game Changers Championship Playoffs, initially scheduled for October 25, 2026 at 5:00 PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Over\" if Team Liquid Brazil and Nova Esports GC play 3 or more maps in this series.\n\nIf fewer than 3 maps are played, this market will resolve to \"Under\".\n\nMaps won by forfeit, disqualification, walkover, or default are counted towards the total, provided that the match is completed.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all for any reason) or ends in a tie, this market will resolve to 50-50.\n\nIf the match is postponed, it must be rescheduled to a start time on or before November 8, 2026 at 11:59 PM ET (14 calendar days after the originally scheduled start of October 25, 2026 at 5:00 PM ET). If, by that deadline, the most recently announced rescheduled start time is on or before the deadline, this market resolves based on the result of the match as played. Otherwise, this market resolves 50-50, regardless of whether the match is subsequently played.\n\nThe match is considered to have begun once live play begins in its first map or game. Warmup rounds and knife rounds do not count as the start of the match. A round forced live because a team did not ready up or resume play within the allotted time does not count as the start of the match if that team forfeits before the next round begins.\n\nIf the match begins and one team wins due to the opponent's match forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, the match will count as completed.\n\nIn that case, any remaining maps required to decide the match, including a map in progress or not yet started, will be counted as won by the winning team.\n\nIf the match ends due to the clinching map being forfeited this will count as a com