8","conditionId":"0xe919ba6c064364de8c249fd4223e2f7be97d7d4e33616b752c5ab95f7b3b7366","question":"Prozorova vs. Garland: Set 1 Games O/U 8.5","slug":"wta-prozoro-garland-2026-10-25-first-set-total-8pt5","sportsMarketType":"tennis_first_set_totals","groupItemTitle":"Guangzhou Open, Qualification: Tatiana Prozorova vs Joanna Garland Set 1 O/U 8.5","line":8.5,"description":"This market refers to the tennis match between Tatiana Prozorova and Joanna Garland in the Guangzhou Open, Qualification, originally scheduled for October 25, 2026 at 1:00AM ET.\nThis market will resolve to \"Over\" if the total number of games completed in the first set equals or exceeds 9. Otherwise, it will resolve to \"Under.\" Any first-set tiebreak counts as one (1) game.\nIf the match is postponed or suspended, this market will remain open until the first set has been completed. A postponement alone will not trigger a 50-50 resolution.\nIf the match is permanently abandoned before the first set is completed, or if the first set has not been completed by November 8, 2026, 11:59 PM ET, this market will resolve 50-50, unless the outcome has already been unconditionally determined based on completed play. An outcome is considered unconditionally determined if it would have been guaranteed under every possible completion of the set played according to the match format published by the tournament organizer for that round, including whether the set is decided by a tiebreak. For example, for a line of 9.5, if play stops with the first set at 5-4, completing the set would have required at least 1 additional game, resulting in at least 10 games played, so \"Over\" would resolve as the winning outcome.\nThe primary resolution source for this market will be official WTA statistics; however, a consensus of credible reporting may also be used.\n\nThis market may resolve only when the listed period of play has concluded and the result can be definitively determined by the listed resolution source(s).","reso